      "updatedAt": "2026-10-11",
      "code": "#include <stdio.h>\n\ndouble average(const int *values, int n) {\n    int sum = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) sum += values[i];\n    return (double)sum / n;\n}\n\nint countAbove(const int *values, int n, double threshold) {\n    int count = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (values[i] > threshold) count++;\n    }\n    return count;\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    int temps[7] = {21, 24, 19, 26, 23, 25, 20};\n    double avg = average(temps, 7);\n    printf(\"avg=%.2f\\n\", avg);\n    printf(\"above=%d\\n\", countAbove(temps, 7, avg));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "expectedOutput": "avg=22.57\nabove=4\n",
      "inputFixtures": {},
      "templateType": "c",
      "sourceLessonId": "c-tutorial-034-lesson"
